cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this model, please cite both the software (this repository, via
  the concept DOI) and the paper. Note the author lists differ: the software
  entry names who wrote the code, the preferred-citation names the paper's
  authors.
title: "bone-mechanostat: a mechanotransduction-resolved multiscale model of bone adaptation"
abstract: >-
  An eight-module multiscale model of bone remodelling that carries a
  mechanical load continuously from organ-level bending, through poroelastic
  lacunocanalicular shear and three-state mechanosensitive channel gating, to
  osteocyte signalling, bone-cell populations, three-surface cortical geometry,
  mineralisation and areal bone mineral density, with systemic
  calcium-PTH-vitamin D coupled bidirectionally. Loading enters as force;
  strain is a regulated output, which preserves the mechanostat feedback loop.
type: software
